W44-PHASE4-S2-validate — production-cell verification of W44-PHASE4-S2-refit
=================================================================================

Bench commit (parent of this work):  2991bb27 (W44-PHASE4-S2-refit; on main@origin)
Bench example:                       jxl-encoder/examples/w44_phase4_s2_validate.rs
Bench TSV:                           benchmarks/w44_phase4_s2_validate_2026-05-24.tsv
Bench script:                        /tmp/run_s2_validate.sh (ephemeral)
Total wall:                          ~5 min on 8-thread CPU encode (18 process invocations)

Hypothesis
----------

Per the W44-PHASE4-S2-refit commit message (`2991bb27`): the post-RECON-DEEP
S1 sweep refit ALL 8/8 strata of the W44-228a per-stratum Tier2Knobs lookup.
L2 distances vs the W44-228a baseline: photo {very_high=1.43, high=1.27,
mid=2.55, low=2.55}, screen {very_high=1.84, high=1.78, mid=1.50, low=1.93}.
The acceptance gate report claimed 36/36 hash-locks BYTE-IDENTICAL (which is
expected — synthetic ≤48² fixtures don't trigger the Tier-2 auto-discriminator
gates on Zenjxl) AND "3 SHIP cells byte-identical".

GAP: hash-lock fixtures don't verify whether production-size cells from the
8 strata produce the new Tier2Knobs outputs as predicted. The S2-refit needed
a per-stratum end-to-end check that the lookup shifts encoded bytes when the
caller opts in via `LossyConfig::with_knobs(Tier2Knobs::auto_for_distance(...))`.

Methodology
-----------

Single-process per cell (each stratum's expansion to RuntimeTuning is unique;
`tuning::runtime::install_or_check_idempotent` is per-process OnceLock so we
cannot batch cells of different strata in one process).

  Mode A = Tier2Knobs::default()
           → expand_to_runtime_tuning() returns RuntimeTuning::default()
           → encode_inner skips install (defaults round-trip)
           → byte-identical to no-knobs encode path

  Mode B = Tier2Knobs::auto_for_distance(class, distance)
           → uses the on-disk W44-PHASE4-S2 lookup table
           → produces NON-default RuntimeTuning for every stratum
           → install fires → encoder takes the override path

For each cell, we encode (with `EncoderStrategy::Zenjxl`, 8 threads,
`butteraugli-loop`+`ssim2-loop` enabled, 8 GiB memory budget) and compute
bfly + ssim2 against the source via jxl-oxide + butteraugli + fast_ssim2
(metadata-immune linear-RGB pipeline per CLAUDE.md guidance).

Cells: one per stratum from CID22-512 (photos) + gb82-sc/graph.png (screens),
plus a W44-228c1 protection spot-check on terminal.png e8 d=4 (the W44-105
SHIP cell the S2-refit commit message specifically claimed byte-identical).

Distance bands (ContentStratum::from_distance_band):
  Low:       d < 1.0    (used d=0.7)
  Mid:       1.0 ≤ d < 2.0  (used d=1.5)
  High:      2.0 ≤ d < 3.5  (used d=3.0)
  VeryHigh:  d ≥ 3.5    (used d=5.0; d=4.0 for terminal W44-228c1 spot-check)

